 <li><strong>Prompt injection:</strong> attacker-controlled text — a web page, an email, a document — manipulates your model into ignoring instructions or leaking data. If your app feeds untrusted content to an LLM, this is your problem.</li>
 <li><strong>Data leakage:</strong> developers paste proprietary code or customer data into chat tools, and that information leaves the organisation's control. Clear internal policies matter as much as tooling.</li>
 <li><strong>Insecure output handling:</strong> treating model output as trusted — executing it, rendering it as HTML, passing it to a shell — turns the model into a bridge for classic injection attacks.</li>
