 <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Is AI-generated code secure?</h3><p>Not automatically. AI can produce vulnerable code or insecure patterns, so you must review, test, and run security checks before merging it.</p><h3>What is prompt injection?</h3><p>An attack where malicious text in an input tricks an AI into ignoring its instructions or taking unintended actions. Validating and sanitizing inputs is the main defense.</p><h3>How do developers secure AI features?</h3><p>Apply least-privilege to agents, validate inputs, scan for leaked secrets, add security tests to CI, and never let AI take sensitive actions without review.</p><h3>What are the biggest AI security risks?</h3><p>Prompt injection, insecure AI-generated code, leaked secrets in prompts or code, and giving agents more permissions than they need.</p><h3>Should I let AI agents run automatically?</h3><p>Only with tight guardrails — limited permissions, logging, and human approval for sensitive actions — since agents take real actions on your systems.</p><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@graph": [{"@type": "BlogPosting", "headline": "AI Security for Developers: Risks & Fixes (2026)", "about": "ai security for developers", "url": "https://studenttimepk.blogspot.com/2026/08/ai-in-dev-why-fixing-vulnerabilities-is.html", "dateModified": "2026-09-15", "author": {"@type": "Organization", "name": "Students Time"}, "publisher": {"@type": "Organization", "name": "Students Time"}}, {"@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Is AI-generated code secure?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Not automatically. AI can produce vulnerable code or insecure patterns, so you must review, test, and run security checks before merging it."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is prompt injection?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "An attack where malicious text in an input tricks an AI into ignoring its instructions or taking unintended actions. Validating and sanitizing inputs is the main defense."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do developers secure AI features?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Apply least-privilege to agents, validate inputs, scan for leaked secrets, add security tests to CI, and never let AI take sensitive actions without review."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What are the biggest AI security risks?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Prompt injection, insecure AI-generated code, leaked secrets in prompts or code, and giving agents more permissions than they need."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Should I let AI agents run automatically?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Only with tight guardrails \u2014 limited permissions, logging, and human approval for sensitive actions \u2014 since agents take real actions on your systems."}}]}]}</script><!--related-guides-->
